    "short_description": "The Ministry of Finance of Egypt is a government agency responsible for managing the national budget, public debt, and fiscal policy. Its mission is to design financial plans, coordinate budgets, and enhance tax revenues to support economic growth and improve the standard of living for citizens. The Ministry is led by Minister Mohamed Maait and is headquartered in the Government District of New Cairo.\n\nThe Ministry provides essential fiscal services, including budget and debt management, tax and customs policy development, and expenditure supervision. It also prepares economic policy frameworks and offers legislative support by drafting financial laws and reviewing legislation from other ministries. The Ministry serves various stakeholders, including the Egyptian government, citizens, and the private sector, ensuring efficient management of public resources and engagement with international financial partners.",
